## What changed
1. `import` line now pulls `readdirSync` from `node:fs`.
2. Runtime table: `claude` and `codex` gained `findTranscript: claudeTranscriptPath` / `codexTranscriptPath`, each with a durable-WHY comment.
3. Session locator section gained three helpers:
   - `findTranscriptFiles(dir, matches, depth)` — walks CLI-owned store folders, matches on file name, unreadable store yields `[]`.
   - `storedTranscriptPath(root, matches, depth)` — returns the resolved path only when exactly one file matches, else `null`.
   - `claudeTranscriptPath` searches `<CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.claude>/projects/` one level deep (`<sessionId>.jsonl`), so `subagents/` helper transcripts one level deeper are never named.
   - `codexTranscriptPath` searches `<CODEX_HOME or ~/.codex>/sessions/` to any depth for names ending `-<sessionId>.jsonl`.
4. `locatorFor` now builds the locator, resolves `transcriptPath` from `runtime.findTranscript` when the runtime has one, and leaves the field out on zero or multiple matches, on non-store runtimes, and on `reportedId === null` (unchanged null contract).

